\ul{
\li{\strong{The guard holds}: 1.567 to 1.446 s in the geometric mean, -7.7 \%, every corpus faster, by 4.1 \% (navier-stokes-euler) to 13.9 \% (reachability); Mathlib 11.11 to 10.35 s; CPU 0.930.}
\li{\strong{Memory}: cslib 2,818 to 2,431 MiB, Mathlib 5,144 to 4,901; Init 811 to 845, the other five within 30 MiB.}
\li{\strong{The sum is less than the product of the parts.} The four changes had given, each against a base of its own and most of them on a busy host, 0.957, 0.976, 0.986 and 0.986 of the base's geometric mean in the executable (the session tables, the loader's second pass, the probe budget, the repeat skip) and 0.912, 0.981, 1.000 and 0.993 on the JVM launcher: products of 0.908 and 0.888, against 0.932 and 0.923 measured together. One part of the difference is known: in the quiet window of section 3 the session tables alone gave 0.968, 0.907 and 0.981 on Init, reachability and con-leche, where their report had 0.963, 0.845 and 0.952 with the other cores busy. The rest was not separated.}
}
}

