}

\ul{
\li{\strong{The published executable} is behind gruszka on six corpora by the wall clock of a warm pass: Init 1.05, Std 1.12, con-leche 1.19, navier-stokes-euler 1.26, cslib 1.06 and Mathlib 1.14 times gruszka's time (12.29 against 10.77 s). It is level on cedar (0.99) and far ahead on reachability (0.21). Before the wave it was, in the same order, at 1.13, 1.19, 1.29, 1.32, 1.17, 1.22, 1.06 and 0.23; the release, on navier-stokes-euler, cslib and Mathlib, at 1.48, 1.29 and 1.35.}
\li{\strong{The published JVM launcher} is ahead of gruszka on six corpora: Init 0.97, Std 0.96, cedar 0.85, reachability 0.15, cslib 0.90 and Mathlib 0.96 (10.35 against 10.77 s). It is behind on con-leche (1.02) and on navier-stokes-euler (1.13). Before the wave it was ahead on cedar, reachability and cslib only.}
\li{\strong{By CPU both are still behind} everywhere but on reachability: the executable needs 1.24 to 1.63 times gruszka's CPU for a pass (Mathlib 95.5 against 64.0 s: 1.49, where it was 1.58), the JVM launcher 1.08 to 1.44 times (Mathlib 79.9 s: 1.25, where it was 1.33). RLVM keeps the 8 cores busier - on Mathlib the executable's 95.5 s of CPU in 12.29 s are 7.8 cores, gruszka's 64.0 s in 10.77 s are 5.9 - so its distance by the wall clock is smaller than by the CPU, and its pass is still bound by the total CPU of the 8 cores. navier-stokes-euler is the largest distance on both launchers and by both measures; what the two checkers do differently there, unit by unit, is [rep-OPT-E](rep-OPT-E).}
\li{\strong{Peak memory}: the executable holds less than gruszka on Init, Std, cedar and reachability (377, 619, 765 and 735 MiB against 527, 659, 798 and 1,223) and more on the four large corpora (con-leche 927 against 832 MiB, navier-stokes-euler 1,515 against 956, cslib 1,624 against 1,509, Mathlib 4,062 against 2,840); the JVM launcher holds more than gruszka on all eight (Mathlib 4,901 MiB).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{7.5 The level fix alone}

\p{The fix of the level store ([rep-INV-1](rep-INV-1), \commit{55f2db3}) was published between the two waves, so the build before this wave has it and the guard above is the wave alone. What the fix itself costs was measured in one more window (21:16:15 to 21:25:43 UTC, 568 s, three corpora one after the other, three interleaved rounds each, the executable with 8 workers): the shared executable of the first wave, which does not have the fix, against the private build of the main tree before the second wave, which has it.}

