\p{The load average of the host carries the measurement itself; what the other cores did is the column after it. Huge pages: the JVM launcher asks for them (\code{\verb~|-XX:+UseTransparentHugePages~}), and [rep-OPT-G](rep-OPT-G) had found that such a request stalls in the kernel's compaction when no free block of 2 MiB is left. The kernel's counter of compaction stalls stood at 6,625,384 before the first window and after the last one, no huge-page fault fell back in any window, and the host had 8,700 to 8,840 free blocks of 2 MiB throughout (17 GiB): no window had to be repeated. The median later pass of every round, in ms (for reachability the mean of the later passes):}

