\subtree{
\title{8. The benchmark rows of the published build, and the optional build}

\p{The rows of [the benchmark tables](rep-benchmarks) were taken again for the published build, in ten quiet-core windows between 21:29 and 21:46 UTC with the other cores idle (0.10 to 0.14 CPUs of the host busy before every window; no compaction stall in any of them): the executable in its default configuration, the JVM launcher, the reference engine by name on the executable, the instruction counts of a cold process in the arena-shaped container for both engines, and the optional executable built with Oracle GraalVM. gruszka and nano-lean were measured again on all eight corpora with their arena run lines and 8 threads, in the same two windows as the executable's rows. The tree was regenerated by \src{bench/track/benchmarks.py} and has every row with its window; the table of the root README was regenerated from the same rows. The summary:}

